M. Lara writes:
 > I have FreeBSD 4.1 on UP1000 motherboard with Alpha 264 CPU, and 3Com590
 > Etherlink III adapter. When i try config this adapter FreeBSD hangs with
 > message:
 > 
 > #ifconfig vx0 inet 10.1.1.100
 > 
 > fatal kernel trap:
 >     trap entry = 0x4    (unaligned access fault)
 >     a0 = 0xfffffe00002f16d2
 >     a1 = 0x28
 >     a2 = 0x11
 >     pc = 0xfffffc0000387a34
 >     ra = 0xfffffc00003879e0
 >     curproc = 0xfffffe00065acb40
 >         pid = 194, comm = ifconfig
 >     panic: trap
 > 
 > On FreeBSD 2.2.x and i386 this adapter work good.

This problem (unaligned access fault) is specific to the alpha.

Can you compile a kernel with debugging enabled (config -g CONFIGFILE)
and map the PC and RA to lines in the source code?  Eg:

	% gdb kernel.debug
	<..>
	(gdb) l *0xfffffc0000387a34

Please crash the machine with the new kernel and use the pc/ra
numbers from the new crash with the new kernel.

The fastest path to getting your machine working might be to get
another network card (3c90x, Intel EtherExpress Pro, a tulip based
cards are known to be good).

Drew


